      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "HTML::FormHandler versions before 0.410002 for Perl render option group labels and radio button labels into HTML without escaping.\n\nThe Select, RadioGroup, CheckboxGroup and HorizCheckboxGroup widgets render a group label unescaped, Select into a label attribute and the other three into element content. RadioGroup also renders each radio button's own label unescaped.\n\nAny application whose option list is built from data rather than literals, using options_from, an options_fieldname method, or the DBIC model, allows attacker-influenced text in a label that can override the options or embed JavaScript in rendered pages.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
